---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import UiHotspotMap from "../components/interactive/UiHotspotMap.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Start Here (Orientation)">
  <main id="content" class="page-main start-here-main" tabindex="-1">
    <header class="page-header">
      <span class="badge badge-ribbon">Quick Orientation</span>
      <h1>Welcome to Publisher → Word</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        If you are transitioning from Microsoft Publisher, you are probably feeling frustrated.
        Things jump across the page, buttons seem to disappear, and nothing stays where you put it.
        <strong>This guide is here to help.</strong>
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="start-here-content">
      <!-- Section 1: The Core Mental Model Shift -->
      <section class="section">
        <h2 class="section-title">Why Does Word Feel So Tricky?</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          In Publisher, every piece of text was inside an independent box. You could drag it around the page or even park it in the grey "scratch area" on the side.
        </p>
        <p class="section-desc">
          In Word, text flows like water in a river. When you drop a photo in, Word treats it like a giant typed character by default. When you press Enter, everything downstream moves forward.
        </p>

        <div class="callout callout-publisher">
          <div class="callout-header">
            <span aria-hidden="true">💡</span>
            <span>Coming from Publisher?</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            You don't have to fight Word! Once you learn to change the <strong>Text Wrap</strong> setting to <span class="badge badge-ribbon">Square</span> or <span class="badge badge-ribbon">In Front of Text</span>, photos and text boxes behave almost exactly like they did in Publisher.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Three Visual Switches (Presented as a balanced 3-card grid) -->
      <section class="section">
        <h2 class="section-title">Three Switches to Turn On Right Now</h2>
        <p class="section-desc">
          Before doing any layout work in Word, turn on these three visual clues to see exactly why objects behave the way they do:
        </p>

        <div class="switches-grid">
          <div class="card switch-card">
            <div class="switch-badge-row">
              <span class="badge badge-ribbon">Switch 1</span>
              <span class="badge badge-contextual">Home Tab</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="switch-title">Show/Hide Formatting (<samp>¶</samp>)</h3>
            <p class="switch-desc">
              Reveals paragraph marks, spaces, tab stops, and the crucial <strong>Object Anchor (⚓)</strong> icon so you can see what is anchoring your pictures.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card switch-card">
            <div class="switch-badge-row">
              <span class="badge badge-ribbon">Switch 2</span>
              <span class="badge badge-contextual">View Tab</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="switch-title">The Page Ruler</h3>
            <p class="switch-desc">
              Displays your exact printable margins and lets you drag paragraph indents and tab positions visually instead of typing centimetre values.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card switch-card">
            <div class="switch-badge-row">
              <span class="badge badge-ribbon">Switch 3</span>
              <span class="badge badge-contextual">Layout Tab → Align</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="switch-title">Alignment Guides</h3>
            <p class="switch-desc">
              Tick <strong>Use Alignment Guides</strong>. Word will automatically display green guidelines when objects line up neatly with page margins or each other.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="callout callout-tip">
          <div class="callout-header">
            <span aria-hidden="true">⚠️</span>
            <span>Watch Out: Disappearing Ribbon Tabs</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            In Word, the tabs for formatting pictures and shapes (like <span class="badge badge-contextual">Picture Format</span> or <span class="badge badge-contextual">Shape Format</span>) only appear at the top of your screen <em>while the object is clicked and selected</em>. If you click away into the blank page, those tabs vanish!
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Interactive Interface Tour -->
      <section class="section tour-section">
        <h2 class="section-title">Interactive Interface Tour</h2>
        <UiHotspotMap />
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Provenance & Background -->
      <section class="section about-section">
        <div class="card about-card">
          <h2 class="section-title">Who Made This Guide?</h2>
          <p class="about-text">
            This guide is an independent project created by Rob Pomeroy to help individuals, schools, charities, and small organisations transition smoothly after Microsoft announced the retirement of Microsoft Publisher.
          </p>
          <p class="about-text">
            It is completely free, carries no ads or sponsored content, and is maintained as a public educational service. To learn more about the author, background, and other open resources, visit <a href="https://pomeroy.me/about/" rel="author">About Rob Pomeroy</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: Next Steps CTA -->
      <section class="section">
        <div class="card next-step-card">
          <div class="next-step-content">
            <span class="badge badge-ribbon">Ready to Begin?</span>
            <h2 class="next-step-title">Start with Lesson 1: How Text Flows</h2>
            <p class="next-step-desc">
              Master how Word flows text and learn why you should never press Enter 15 times to reach the next page.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="next-step-action">
            <a href="/lessons/01-how-text-flows" class="btn btn-primary">
              <span>Go to Lesson 1</span>
              <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    margin-block-end: var(--space-8);
    padding-block-end: var(--space-6);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    line-height: var(--line-height-normal);
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
  }

  .start-here-content {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-10);
  }

  .section {
    width: 100%;
  }

  .section-title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--ink-primary);
  }

  .section-desc {
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    color: var(--ink-primary);
    line-height: var(--line-height-normal);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-4);
  }

  /* 3-Card Grid for Visual Switches */
  .switches-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 19rem), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-block: var(--space-5);
  }

  .switch-card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    padding: var(--space-5);
    background-color: var(--surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 3px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 4%);
  }

  .switch-badge-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-3);
  }

  .switch-title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2) 0;
    color: var(--ink-primary);
  }

  .switch-desc {
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin: 0;
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  /* About Card */
  .about-card {
    padding: var(--space-6);
    background-color: var(--surface-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  .about-text {
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    line-height: var(--line-height-normal);
    color: var(--ink-primary);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-3);
  }

  .about-text:last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }

  /* Next Step Banner Card */
  .next-step-card {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    background-color: var(--surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-ui);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 4px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 5%);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .next-step-card {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
    }
  }

  .next-step-title {
    font-size: var(--font-size-2xl);
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 var(--space-2) 0;
    color: var(--ink-primary);
  }

  .next-step-desc {
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
    margin: 0;
    max-inline-size: var(--max-prose-width);
  }
</style>
